# Spells reviewed in the full pass over arcane spells (Impossible Magic, Feybound, Lost Omens, adventure paths and older books).
# Same format as spell_evals: s(name, ratings [Damage, Control, Debuff, Buff/Heal, Positioning, Utility], grades [spellbook, scroll, wand], eval)
from spell_evals_base import s

# rank 1
s('Propelling Air Stream', '200030', 'BCD', "Propelling Air Stream is an attack spell, so through Spellstrike its 2d6 bludgeoning per rank lands on the weapon's attack roll, and whether or not the Strike hits, Cyrus gains a 15-foot fly Speed until the end of his next turn. That makes it a payload that also reaches a flying enemy, crosses a gap or climbs a wall in the same turn. Briny Bolt does the same damage with a better rider, so this is the pick when the fight needs height.")

# rank 2
s('Spray of Salt', '310000', 'BDD', "Spray of Salt is the strongest Fortitude area damage at rank 2: a 15-foot cone of 5d4 acid, half on a successful save, rising by 2d4 per rank. Through Expansive Spellstrike from reach the cone starts beside the target and can be aimed away from the party. Acid is rarely resisted, skeletons included, and creatures with the unholy, ooze or water trait that fail also take persistent spirit damage. It gives the rank-2 slot a Fortitude option alongside Acid Grip and Shockwave.")
s('Blood Runs Cold', '112000', 'BDD', "Blood Runs Cold deals persistent cold damage with a Fortitude save, and a failure leaves the target slowed 1 for a round; a critical failure keeps it slowed until the persistent damage ends. It isn't limited to living creatures, so it works on undead. As a Spellstrike payload it is a single-target way to take an action away from a low-Fortitude enemy such as a caster or skirmisher. The damage itself is small and only grows every two ranks.")
s('Unrelenting Gravity', '030020', 'BDD', "Unrelenting Gravity knocks the target prone on a failed Fortitude save and leaves it encumbered for a round, which slows it by 10 feet and makes it clumsy. Prone enemies are off-guard and must spend an action to stand, and a flying creature that fails falls. From rank 4 it targets up to five creatures. It is a reliable Fortitude control payload, though Shockwave already knocks a whole cone prone on a Reflex save.")
s('Disorienting Flash', '202000', 'BDD', "Disorienting Flash deals sonic damage with a basic Fortitude save. Cast with 2 actions it is a 10-foot burst of 2d10, and creatures that fail are dazzled. Through Expansive Spellstrike the burst is centred on a corner of the target's square, covering a 20-foot square, so it often catches allies in melee. It is a basic-save alternative to Noise Blast, with dazzle in place of stun.")

# rank 3
s('Roaring Applause', '023000', 'ADD', "On a successful Will save the target still can't use reactions while Cyrus sustains it, for up to 10 minutes; on a failure it is also slowed 1, and its applause gains the manipulate trait at the start of its turn, which triggers Reactive Strike from anyone who threatens it. It has no incapacitation trait, so it works on bosses. It is a mental effect, so mindless creatures such as zombies and skeletons are immune; undead that think, such as ghouls, wights and vampires, are affected. Sustaining costs Cyrus one action a turn, which is worth it against a single strong enemy. From rank 6 it targets up to 10 creatures.")
s('Gravity Wave', '330000', 'ADD', "Gravity Wave is a 30-foot cone of 6d4 bludgeoning damage with a Fortitude save, and creatures that fail are knocked prone. Through Expansive Spellstrike the cone starts beside the target and runs 30 feet past it. It pairs damage and prone with a Fortitude save, so it covers enemies with high Reflex that Shockwave and Lightning Bolt struggle with, and bludgeoning isn't resisted by skeletons.")
s('Skyglass Prison', '050000', 'ADD', "Skyglass Prison immobilizes the target on a failed Fortitude save until it Escapes or breaks the cage, and even a successful save immobilizes it until the start of Cyrus's next turn. A critical failure restrains it. Through Spellstrike, an immobilized enemy can't close the distance to Cyrus's reach or chase a fleeing ally, and escaping costs it actions. Few rank-3 spells have a success effect this strong.")
s('Lightning Lasso', '230000', 'BDD', "Lightning Lasso deals 2d12 electricity on a Reflex save, and a failure immobilizes the target until the end of Cyrus's next turn. Sustaining it keeps the target immobilized and deals more damage, but that costs an action Cyrus usually needs for recharging. Without sustaining it is a Reflex payload with a strong failure effect.")
s('Rend Magic', '301000', 'BDD', "Rend Magic is an attack spell dealing 3d10 force damage on the weapon's attack roll, and the target then takes more force damage each time it casts a spell for a minute. Force damage gets past the resistances of ghosts and shadows, which suits this campaign, and the follow-up punishes enemy casters. Briny Bolt does a little more damage at rank 3, so this is the payload for casters and incorporeal enemies.")
s('Tricks and Treats', '022000', 'BDD', "Tricks and Treats affects every enemy within 10 feet of Cyrus. On a failed Will save a creature can't use reactions until the start of its next turn and is clumsy 1 for a minute; a success still makes it clumsy 1 for a round. The area is an emanation around Cyrus, which Expansive Spellstrike doesn't expand, so it is cast directly. It is one of the few ways to deny reactions to several enemies at rank 3.")

# rank 4
s('Freezing Touch', '240000', 'ADD', "Freezing Touch deals 5d4 persistent cold damage with a Fortitude save, and a failure immobilizes the target for a minute or until it Escapes; a critical failure also leaves it off-guard while immobilized. Its touch range becomes the weapon's reach through Spellstrike. A long immobilize on a Fortitude save is strong control for a reach fighter, since the target can't close the distance or chase allies.")
s('Friends to Foes', '304000', 'ADD', "Friends to Foes deals 6d6 mental damage with a Will save and leaves the target frightened 1, or frightened 2 on a failure. The frightened condition can't drop while the target is within 10 feet of an ally, and on a failure it can't move closer to its allies, which breaks up formations. As a Will payload it combines solid damage with a lasting debuff.")
s('Lost Things Returned', '041000', 'ADD', "Lost Things Returned leaves the target slowed 1 for a round even on a successful Will save, and for a minute on a failure; a critical failure also stops it using reactions. An ally can attack the illusion to end the spell for 5d10 mental damage. A slow on a successful save makes it one of the most reliable action-denial spells at rank 4.")
s('Gift of Dusk', '003000', 'BDD', "Gift of Dusk enfeebles the target on a Fortitude save: enfeebled 1 for a minute on a success, and a curse that starts at enfeebled 2 on a failure. If the curse reaches its last stage, the target's shadow becomes a creature that fights for Cyrus. It needs a target with a shadow and carries the unholy trait. Enfeebled lowers an enemy's damage and Athletics, which makes it a useful debuff against a heavy hitter.")
s('Unending Tears', '003000', 'CDD', "Unending Tears dazzles the target even on a successful Will save, until it spends an action to clear its eyes. A failure adds stupefied 1 and suppresses an emotion effect on it. It works through Spellstrike as a Will debuff, but Briny Bolt blinds rather than dazzles on the weapon's attack roll, so this is a fallback.")

# rank 5
s('Plasma Whirl', '402000', 'ADD', "Plasma Whirl cast with 2 actions is a 30-foot cone of 5d6 electricity and 5d6 fire with a basic Reflex save, and creatures that fail are sickened 1, or sickened 2 on a critical failure. Through Expansive Spellstrike the cone starts beside the target and covers a large group. The two damage types are resisted separately, but the average of about 35 damage in a 30-foot cone with a sickened rider makes it one of the strongest rank-5 area payloads.")
s('Crucible of Iron', '123000', 'BDD', "Crucible of Iron dazzles the target and deals persistent fire damage even on a successful Reflex save. A failure adds enfeebled 1 for a minute or until it Escapes, and a critical failure makes it enfeebled 2 and immobilized. It is a solid single-target debuff payload on a Reflex save.")

# rank 6
s('Curse of the Toad Prince', '050000', 'ABD', "Curse of the Toad Prince only targets humanoids and has the incapacitation trait, so it works fully on creatures of level 12 or lower. Even on a successful Will save the target is sickened 1 and drops everything it is holding, which disarms a weapon user or a caster with a staff. On a failure it becomes a harmless toad for a minute. Against humanoid enemies such as knights, cultists and casters, it is one of the strongest rank-6 payloads.")
s('Proximal Shift', '200040', 'BCD', "Proximal Shift teleports Cyrus up to 60 feet, knocking prone the creatures he leaves beside him if they fail a Reflex save, and dealing 6d6 bludgeoning to creatures next to where he arrives. It moves him into position and deals area damage in one 2-action cast, which suits Laughing Shadow, but it isn't a Spellstrike payload.")

# rank 7
s('Puppet Strings', '140000', 'BDD', "Puppet Strings has the incapacitation trait. On a failed Reflex save the target is clumsy 1 and slowed 1, and each time Cyrus casts or sustains it he can make the target Stride or Strike one of its allies. The target can end it with a Fortitude save at the end of each turn, and sustaining costs an action. It is strong control against a creature of level 14 or lower.")
s('Spell Turning', '000400', 'BBD', "Spell Turning lasts an hour and lets Cyrus use his reaction to counteract a spell that targets him, turning it back on its caster if the counteract succeeds. It is a legacy spell that wasn't renamed. It only works on targeted spells, not areas, and ends after one use, so it is a good pre-cast before a fight with an enemy caster.")

# rank 8
s('Metallic Meteorite Glyph', '500000', 'BDD', "Metallic Meteorite Glyph deals 8d12 bludgeoning damage with a basic Reflex save, about 52 on average, to one target when cast with 2 actions. As a Spellstrike payload it is high single-target damage that still lands when the Strike misses. With 3 actions it hits up to three creatures, but that isn't usable through Spellstrike.")

# rank 9
s('Weird', '503000', 'BDD', "Weird is a legacy spell that deals 16d6 mental damage to any number of creatures within 120 feet with a Will save, leaving them frightened, and critical failures risk death. It is very strong, but it is rank 9, which Cyrus only reaches at level 17.")

# promoted from the passed-over list
s('Ignite Fireworks', '202000', 'BCD', "Ignite Fireworks deals 1d8 fire and 1d8 sonic damage in a 10-foot burst on a Reflex save, and dazzles creatures even when they succeed: for 1 round on a success, 3 rounds on a failure and a minute on a critical failure. Dazzled enemies treat everyone as concealed, so their attacks need a flat check. Through Expansive Spellstrike the burst is centred on a corner of the target's square and covers a 20-foot square, which often catches allies in melee; cast directly at 60 feet it can be placed clear of them. Revealing Light dazzles for longer and also counters invisibility, while this one adds damage.")
s('Scouring Pulse', '402003', 'ACD', "Scouring Pulse deals 6d8 vitality damage with a basic Reflex save in a 10-foot-radius cylinder up to 120 feet away, and creatures that fail take persistent vitality damage and glow, which stops them being concealed and makes invisible ones only concealed. Vitality damage only harms undead and creatures healed by void energy, so it can be dropped on a melee with Mira and Cassius in it without hurting them. It is cast directly rather than through Spellstrike, since Expansive Spellstrike doesn't expand a cylinder. In a campaign against hordes of undead, it is one of Cyrus's best area spells at rank 5.")

# changes after review
s('Blazing Bolt', '400000', 'BDD', "Through Spellstrike, Blazing Bolt uses its two-action version: 4d6 fire on the weapon's attack roll at rank 2, rising by 2d6 per rank. Briny Bolt deals the same damage per rank as bludgeoning, which is resisted less often than fire, and also blinds, so Blazing Bolt is never his best attack payload. Cast directly with 3 actions it fires rays at three enemies, but those use his spell attack, which stays trained until level 9, and the turn neither recharges Spellstrike nor uses Expansive Spellstrike. It is a fallback for a turn when he can't reach melee and three enemies are spread out.")
s('Laughing Fit', '022000', 'BDD', "Laughing Fit stops the target's reactions even on a successful save, and a failure also slows it. It only targets living creatures, so it does nothing to undead, which this campaign is full of. It must be sustained each turn, which takes an action Cyrus usually needs to recharge or move. From level 5, Roaring Applause does the same job on any creature that isn't mindless, undead included, and also sets up Reactive Strike, so Laughing Fit is best left to a scroll.")
s('Revealing Light', '012003', 'BAC', "Revealing Light dazzles creatures in a 10-foot burst for 2 rounds even on a successful Reflex save, a minute on a failure and 10 minutes on a critical failure. It also makes invisible creatures concealed and removes other concealment, so the whole party can target them, which matters against shadows, ghosts and hidden casters. Through Expansive Spellstrike the burst covers a 20-foot square on a corner of the target and can catch allies, so it is often better cast directly at range 120 feet.")
